{
  "note": "Argument validation defects confirmed by the IronCalc differential harness. This engine never checks argument count or argument type: `FUNCTIONS[name](args)` is called with whatever the parser collected, so a missing argument becomes `undefined` and coerces to 0. Excel and Google Sheets refuse these formulas outright; the corpus records a refusal as `#ERROR!`, matching the convention in syntax.json.",
